# JSONEncoder.default() previously called o.timetuple() for all date/datetime
# objects, which strips timezone information. For timezone-aware datetimes this
# caused http_date() to treat the local time as UTC, producing a wrong offset.

# When o is a datetime with tzinfo set, call o.astimezone(timezone.utc) to
# convert to UTC first, then pass the datetime object directly to http_date()
# instead of a struct_time.

# Files changed:
# flask/json/__init__.py             - JSONEncoder.default() aware-datetime branch
# tests/test_json_datetime_issue.py  - new regression test for the fix

# Verification:
# Construct a Sydney-time datetime (+10:00) and assert that its JSON
# serialization equals that of the equivalent naive UTC datetime
# (2017-01-01 02:00:00). Before the fix the two values differed because the
# aware datetime was serialised as 12:00:00+00:00 instead of 02:00:00+00:00.
# pytest tests/test_json_datetime_issue.py  → 1 passed

